# exit Pi to the guest shell
pi                  # new native process; no inherited Gemini/model/resume flags
pi -c               # fresh native latest-session continuation
pi -r               # native picker; no preselected session fabricated by Sandpi
```

Only the initial process consumes Sandpi-only launch policy such as
`--tool-profile`, `--resume-fallback` and explicit recovery intent. The marker is
removed before exec. A later Pi process derives model/thinking/tool state from its
own arguments and native session, not from the process that happened to boot the
room. Prompt text, file arguments and system-prompt contents never enter the
invocation record.

Plain `sandpi` can enter a room without canonical Sandcodex credentials, allowing
Pi-native/custom providers configured inside that room. Explicit provider
shortcuts remain strict because selecting one is a claim that its shared canonical
route is available.

