OpenRouter's catalog can describe reasoning in three materially different ways:

| Catalog evidence | Sandpi behavior |
|---|---|
| Explicit `supported_efforts` array | Expose exactly those positive levels; expose `off` only when reasoning is optional. |
| `supported_efforts: null` | Treat the gateway as accepting its complete effort vocabulary, still respecting mandatory/default metadata. |
| Reasoning metadata without a selector | Provider-managed reasoning; usable without `--thinking`, but Sandpi does not invent a Pi picker. |
| Malformed selector | Preserve visibility for diagnosis, reject explicit managed effort and automatic qualification. |

```bash
