the VM. The Pi extension repeats that check against the model actually restored or
selected on session start, native resume, tree navigation and later model changes.
It also compares Pi's active thinking level to the requested level. This second
check matters because Pi normally clamps an unavailable level by searching
stronger levels before weaker ones. Sandpi refuses the mismatch before inference
instead of silently turning `medium` into `high`, or otherwise changing the request.

