sandpi openrouter --models 'openrouter/*'       # explicit scope; no automatic test
sandpi openrouter --skip-ladder                # explicit ungraded automatic pick
sandpi benchmark list
sandpi benchmark run --model VENDOR/EXACT_FREE_ID --course ladder --trials 3
sandpi benchmark report
```

The bounded cold selection is convenience, not an intelligence ranking. Catalog
reasoning/context metadata is only capability and deterministic ordering evidence
for ungraded candidates; it is not a quality score.
A pass is provisional until each covered rung has three consecutive passes. The
floor is the contiguous passing prefix, not an average hiding a broken earlier
rung. Latest scored failures lower the floor; infrastructure failures do not erase
a prior quality result. Cached grades expire after 30 days or model metadata,
Pi pin, adapter, course or default-budget profile changes. Custom budgets produce
inspectable receipts but do not automatically qualify the default profile.

Every probe has fresh synthetic files, a separate Pi agent directory, no saved
session, no project context discovery and only read/bash/edit/write. It cannot
become the latest work conversation or mutate the live project by accident in the
benchmark adapter. The ordinary agent-owned guest still has its normal authority
and network: a deliberately adversarial root agent could inspect the course or
forge in-guest observations. This is an execution-grounded advisory, not tamper-
proof certification. The host accepts bounded validated metadata, never executes
candidate Python, and does not archive raw prompts or completions in grade records.

Success requires exact provider/model identity, actual completed native tools,
settled assistant output, functional checks and integrity checks. Saying “fixed”
is not a pass. Provider errors/timeouts/budget exhaustion are unscored. A complete
attempt with incorrect code is a scored failure. Benchmark execution refuses
bare-metal; previously cached grades or explicit selection remain usable there.

