# Current-context input-cost lens — rev0075 / Sounding

## Purpose

`/sandmodels` already compares configured per-million-token rates. Sounding adds a
more concrete, still conservative question to the existing overview, details view,
and exact `--inspect` report:

> At Pi's current context estimate, what would the configured input-token component
> look like on the current model and this candidate if both used the same token count?

No command, flag, preference, provider request, model rank, budget rule or automatic
selection is added.

## Usage

The normal commands are unchanged:

```text
/sandmodels
/sandmodels paid --max-output 5
/sandmodels paid --inspect vendor/model
/sandmodels all --tools --fits --details
```

After an eligible candidate is selected or named, the report includes one line such
as this synthetic example:

```text
Current-context input scenario (~20000 current Pi-estimated tokens; same token count; candidate tokenization is not estimated): ordinary-input component $0.04 -> $0.12; all-cache-read component $0.004 -> $0.012. Tier basis: current base rate; selected tier above 10000 tokens. Cache reuse/mix, output, reasoning and other charges are not predicted.
```

The figures are USD components derived from Pi's effective registered `model.cost`
metadata, whose rates are expressed per million tokens. They do not come from an
account lookup or a provider request.

## Calculation

For each comparable OpenRouter model:

1. Read Pi's current context estimate only when it is known and belongs to the
   current effective model's context window.
2. Reuse that one token count for the current model and candidate.
3. Resolve the configured base rate or the last matching prompt-length tier.
   A tier applies only when the token count is **strictly greater** than its
   `inputTokensAbove` threshold.
4. Display two separate arithmetic components:
   - ordinary input: `tokens × configured input rate / 1,000,000`
   - all-cache-read: `tokens × configured cache-read rate / 1,000,000`

Zero is a known value. Tiny positive components remain visibly positive. Invalid,
missing or malformed usage/rates remain unknown. A current model outside OpenRouter
is labeled not comparable rather than assigned a zero account price.

The implementation reuses Sandpi's bounded cost reader. It does not inspect model
headers, credentials, account balances, request payloads, message text or token data.
It does not mutate the model, tier rows or context object.

## What the scenario does not predict

The current estimate was produced for the active model. Different models can use
different native tokenizers, adapters, system prompts and transformations. The
candidate's actual prompt count can therefore differ even before new user input.
The same-token-count comparison is deliberate and explicitly disclosed.

The line also does not predict:

- whether any tokens will be cache hits, cache writes or ordinary input;
- whether a cache survives a model/provider/endpoint switch;
- the next user's input, tool results, attachments or request hooks;
- output, reasoning, image, web-search, per-request or other charges;
- time-window/weekday pricing that Pi's static tier structure cannot represent;
- endpoint selection, provider availability, account policy, taxes or credits;
- a request total, session budget, maximum bill, savings percentage or quality.

Use `/sandcost` for provider-reported observations after requests. Reported usage
uses the selected model's native tokenizer and can include actual account charge,
reasoning and cached-token fields. That observed evidence remains separate from the
picker's configured scenario.

## Unknown and stale state

Pi deliberately reports context tokens as unknown immediately after compaction
until suitable post-compaction usage exists. Sounding preserves that state:

```text
Current-context input scenario: unknown because Pi context usage is unavailable; unknown is not zero.
```

No percentage or context-window fraction is converted back into a fake count.

The complete preview continues to guard confirmation. If context usage changes,
including crossing a configured pricing tier, the final rerender differs and the
pending switch is declined. This is a stale-dialog check, not an atomic lock over
tokenization, catalog metadata, account pricing or the outgoing request.

## Side effects and ownership

Rendering the line adds no inference, credential lookup, credit probe, catalog
refresh, compaction, cache probe, model switch, paid grant, settings write, editor
change or conversation entry. It is emitted in the same UI-only notification as the
existing comparison. `--inspect` remains read-only. An unchanged normal confirmation
still delegates the exact current registered candidate to Pi.

Free-first discovery, rate filters, sorting, routing comparison, thinking inputs,
image awareness and explicit paid permission are unchanged. The scenario is not
used for eligibility or ordering.

## Verification scope

Local tests cover strict tier boundaries, sorted tier application, zero/unknown/
malformed inputs, non-OpenRouter current models, tiny display values, overview and
details disclosure, immutability, command integration and tier-crossing stale
confirmation. Exact-parent comparisons separate the new disclosure/guard behavior
from preserved picker controls.

The supplied native comparison audit now requires the scenario label while retaining
its outer no-inference and unchanged-state guards. It remains **NOT RUN** against the
installed pinned Pi in this release environment.

Manual native exercises, also **NOT RUN**:

1. With known context usage, inspect a free model, a paid model with permission off,
