For the single-request rejection the existing static request-guidance renderer
points to `/sanddefaults` and `/sandpi help access`. It explains the estimated
cost versus the whole in-flight budget and that waiting alone is insufficient.
It does not copy the provider message or hint into conversation logs. It does not
promise a refund, zero charge, a particular smaller allowance, or a fitting price.

The selected model, prompt, reasoning, maxTokens, catalog, native settings and
paid permission are not modified. There is no automatic compaction, prompt
truncation, reduced output request, top-up suggestion disguised as authorization,
model substitution, retry timer or newly enabled fallback. Native requests and
provider policy remain owned by their existing layers.

Partial content, opaque reasoning signatures and already-observed usage remain
available. Missing accounting stays missing rather than zero. The classification
uses the existing host `request` outcome; its private fixed reason is not added
to host release fields, a new ledger or a credential record. Existing cooldowns
are neither created nor healed by the request-local outcome.

