Waits already supplied through onResponse, or scalar retry_after / retryAfter
metadata (including the recognized metadata header maps), can reach the existing
cooldown handling. Conflicting or malformed hints are omitted rather than guessed.
The existing 24-hour bound and scheduler policy are unchanged.

This does not recover HTTP headers that the native SDK has discarded. In the
pinned adapters, onResponse runs only after successful client response creation;
non-2xx SDK errors may therefore omit Retry-After from the observable result.
The acceptance fixture deliberately supplies a synthetic metadata hint. It is
not evidence that every real endpoint supplies one there. No fetch interception,
transport replacement, extra polling, or inference call was added to obtain it.

