Both templates are declared in `@sandpi/core/package.json` and copied into its Nix
package. They are not executable slash-command handlers, system-prompt patches,
or every-turn injections. Native prompt expansion supplies the optional focus.

Use native `pi config` resource selection to disable either template. The existing
native package `prompts` filter (including `[]`) now survives wrapper reconciliation
and a managed package-path upgrade. The current-path declaration takes precedence
over a stale previous-path declaration. The credential/provider extension remains
mandatory; disabling prompts does not disable it. No new settings schema is added.
Project resource trust and `--no-prompt-templates` remain native policy.

These packaged templates are immutable defaults. Put your own versions under
distinct names in native user/project prompt directories. Do not rely on a name
collision to override a bundled prompt; native discovery decides collisions.

