One native `custom` entry uses customType `sandpi.landing-note` and exactly:

```json
{"schema":"sandpi.landing-note.v1","text":"Next: inspect parser.ts; tests not run."}
```

The latest matching entry on the active parent chain wins. An empty text is a
clearing marker; clear is not erasure. Previous versions remain in session
history and copies. Tree navigation can reveal an older note or no note; sibling
branches are not searched. Native fork/clone can retain notes with their ancestry.
