| Observation | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Context ceiling | Current model metadata known to Pi, not a measured coding-quality limit. |
| Context usage | Pi's estimate for that window; absent, null or stale-window data stays unknown. |
| Compaction reserve and recent retention | Resolved independently using the exact model override, ordinary setting, then native default. |
| Compaction threshold | Window minus reserve; explicitly inactive when automatic compaction is off. |
| Numeric sampling | Recognized model defaults after the actual thinking level's per-field overrides. |

The settings are already merged by Pi before the report resolves exact model
values. Native defaults are reserve 16,384 and recent retention 20,000 when no
more specific values apply. A reserve also affects summary output limits; it is
not simply a convenient knob for choosing an earlier compaction point. `/compact`
can itself use a billable request. This revision does not change those values or
run compaction for you. [R3, R4]

The sampler report is deliberately modest. It shows recognized finite numeric
fields such as temperature and top_p, not arbitrary configuration objects.
