The model-specific recipe table remains in `src/pi/model-defaults.json`. No
recipes or review dates were changed for this release. GPT/Gemini and paid models
still bypass the small-model coding ladder; unreviewed paid models remain usable.

The new `src/pi/model-settings.mjs` is a pure presentation helper, independent of
recipes, credentials, streams, accounting and the VM. If Pi gains an equivalent
native report, remove the helper and its call from `/sanddefaults`. No migration
of conversations or accounting records is needed.

No synthetic “effective intelligence window,” blanket temperature choice,
maximum-effort mandate, automatic model switching, or context-rewriting extension
was added. A tool that exposes the current settings and then respects the next
choice is more useful here than another hidden automatic policy.

