The existing ladder's `select_exact` helper replaces real --provider, --model and
--models options with the same exact-selection prefix as before. It now preserves
all other arguments in order, including literal selectors after `--`, selectors
inside other options' values, whitespace, Unicode, empty strings, @files and shell
metacharacters. It does not mutate the caller's list, split strings, evaluate
commands, resolve files or log their contents.

This applies both to a cached coding pass, a successful existing qualification,
and the host's explicit --skip-ladder path. The old scanner could drop literal
text regardless of which path selected a model. The fix does not change catalog
ordering, score requirements, the number of qualification candidates, retries,
provider requests or accounting within that pre-existing workflow.

**Restoring the default can restore its existing model calls.** On the explicit
