An eligible ID uses the same current effective model, registered candidate,
settings/context projections, the current-context input-cost scenario, image-tag counter, thinking inputs, routing
preferences, prices, compaction, recipes and cautions as the normal picker.
The default is the existing overview; `--details` uses the full existing renderer.
The report is wrapped in an explicit **candidate, not a selection** banner and
**snapshot only / no switch requested** ending. The reused `Selected:` label means
the candidate described by that report, not an already-applied model choice.

The handler never opens select/confirm/editor, waits for idle, acquires/releases
shared dialog ownership, reads or writes an editor draft, appends a session entry,
calls a model/thinking/tool setter, or requests inference/auth/credit/catalog data.
There is no deferred action: this inspection will never switch models later.
Normal `/sandmodels` still owns its dialogs and complete post-confirmation guard;
its original final comparison/commit block is unchanged.

In TUI/RPC the report uses `notify`, outside normal model context. With no UI the
handler writes human-readable text to stderr, not a new JSON protocol or stdout
model response. RPC clients need no dialog response for inspection, but native
notifications have no acknowledgement. The presence of output is not proof of
terminal rendering. Invocation of an unloaded slash command is not a guaranteed
local action. Tests of handlers do not establish native print-mode dispatch.

