| Native Pi `models.json` | Your final exact-model metadata overrides, composed by Pi itself after provider registration. |
| Native Pi request adapter | Per-request conversion and any further context/reasoning output adjustment. |
| Provider endpoint | Actual acceptance, output and billing. A metadata ceiling is not a guarantee. |

Missing upstream `max_completion_tokens` retains the preexisting conservative
normalizer fallback (at most 8,192 and bounded by context). This revision does not
invent a large capacity when the catalog is silent. OpenRouter endpoint capacities
can differ; native request clamping can lower the actual transmitted output cap.
A large configured window is not a benchmark of useful coding context.

Malformed managed capacity/input fields stop registration instead of falling
back silently to older native numbers. Native user overrides are validated by Pi;
Sandpi does not reinterpret or repair those settings here.

