## The workflow

Use the existing `/sandmodels` command from a native Pi session. Choose a scoped,
filtered list, inspect the exact candidate, and confirm the switch. Cancelling
either dialog leaves model selection, settings and conversation history unchanged. Native `/model` remains the direct, unmodified path.

```text
/sandmodels
/sandmodels paid --reviewed
/sandmodels all --tools --fits
/sandmodels paid kimi
/sandmodels all --vision
/sandmodels --help
```

The first optional word is `free`, `paid`, or `all`; the default is `free` even
when this process has paid permission. Remaining ordinary words match IDs, display
names, and currently applicable recipe names/roles, case-insensitively. All words
must match. This is substring search, not shell expansion or a fuzzy successor
resolver. An ID containing `:free` remains that exact ID.

Filters combine with AND semantics:

| Filter | Required evidence |
| --- | --- |
| `--tools` | Explicit `true` in Sandpi's validated catalog tool capability |
| `--vision` | `image` in the effective native Pi model's input array |
| `--fits` | Known current Pi context estimate, known candidate compaction settings, and positive headroom below its threshold |
| `--reviewed` | A currently applicable Sandpi recipe under the existing canonical-revision and review-window checks |

Unknown flags fail visibly rather than falling back to an unfiltered picker.
Search is bounded to 512 characters and 32 words/filters/values. Tab completion
offers sections, filters and sort values without discarding earlier search terms.

By default, free choices keep the established order, including degraded routes
last and currently unavailable models omitted. Large lists show five model choices per page
with previous/next controls; paging itself does not switch anything. The all view appends cached paid choices;
by default it is not a cheapest-first sort or a new quality ranking. Explicit
ordering is described below; unavailable free models remain omitted in every order. Ungraded free models and
unreviewed paid models remain available without the corresponding filter.

