validated OpenRouter catalog-added timestamp is within that many 24-hour periods
of the loaded snapshot's fetch time. The exact boundary is inclusive. Unknown
timestamps or unknown snapshot time fail this filter; without it they remain
selectable.

`--sort newest` orders known timestamps descending, leaves equal timestamps in the
existing order, and places unknowns last. It is opt-in. Plain `/sandmodels` and
`--sort default` retain the prior free-first, route-aware ordering. This local sort
mirrors the meaning OpenRouter documents for its own `newest` catalog sort, but it
does not issue a live API request.

