the native picker. Neither creates a Sandpi transcript or external session format.

The managed policy is now an immutable Pi package, `@sandpi/core`, loaded through
Pi's package system. The room's writable `~/.pi/agent` remains available for
personal packages, settings, MCP servers, skills, prompts and themes. A migration
archives the earlier copied extension so only one provider wrapper and one set of
commands are active.

Launch facts are read from an external fixed-schema runtime document. Custom Pi
entries still store branch-local profile, physical transport, handoff and affinity
facts that belong with the session, but prompts and tool output never enter the
host observation index.

Resume preflight is deliberately narrow. It asks Pi's exported SessionManager for
the active branch projection before startup fallback can hide the saved model. It
exists for exact-model continuity, Gemini key affinity, missing-model policy and
headless operation. Human TUI session choice, branch movement and ordinary model
switching remain Pi-native.

The guest wrapper protects composition rather than tool authority. `pi
--no-extensions` remains valid and loads only the reviewed package explicitly;
normal `pi`, `pi -c`, `pi -r`, `/reload`, and package commands use Pi's native
resource loader.

