# Pi process runtime lifetime

Rev0038 / Hearth. No new user command or setting.

## The failure this prevents

Every wrapped Pi invocation has a small, process-local runtime document. The
managed extension reads it when its factory loads, including after native
`/reload`. Rev0037 kept only the newest 31 documents before making a new one,
without checking whether older documents still belonged to live processes.
A single long-running conversation plus 40 short commands could therefore lose
its configuration before its next reload. It did not require 32 concurrent
conversations. Pi session JSONL itself was not deleted by this cleanup.

## Process lifetime, not recency

New filenames carry the Linux boot ID, PID, process start ticks and a random
suffix. The existing Python-to-Nix-to-Pi exec chain retains process identity.
No process arguments, environment, runtime JSON contents, or conversations are
