# A one-shot spend notice, not a budget — rev0048

## Use the existing cost workflow

```text
/sandcost
/sandcost models
/sandcost watch 2.50
/sandcost watch
/sandcost watch off
/sandcost help
```

Off by default. The amount is a positive plain decimal in **OpenRouter credits**,
from 0.00000001 through 1000000000, with up to eight decimal places. Currency
symbols, exponents, negative amounts, zero, extra arguments and controls are
rejected without changing the notice. Invalid arguments now produce an error
instead of being silently ignored by the old report. Help/off do not read entries.
Off neither changes paid permission nor erases existing observations.

The threshold applies to the existing **session-file subtotal**, including other
branches and inherited history. It is NOT additional spending since arming.
Existing charges can trigger an immediate notification. The plain report retains
active-branch and session-file totals and adds one quiet state/discovery line when
off. No threshold is chosen automatically.

While armed, check after Pi's whole agent run settles (including aborts), or on
explicit /sandcost, /sandcost models, or /sandcost watch inspection. An entire tool/retry/continuation
run may exceed the threshold first. No per-token/request check or preauthorization.
Manual compaction may need a later /sandcost inspection. This is not a watcher of
every provider operation. One notification is attempted per explicit arming;
status/help/plain report do not re-arm. watch AMOUNT explicitly replaces/re-arms.

`/sandcost models` is another explicit inspection of the same session-file
subtotal. It can consume an already-crossed notice once, then shows the resulting
notice state. It does not choose or re-arm a threshold. Its model groups are evidence
presentation, not separate ledgers whose totals should be added to `/sandcost`.

## What the number means

Reuse summarizeUsage and existing sandpi.openrouter-usage.v1 entries. No new ledger,
stream hook, schema, running charge accumulator, historical backfill, native cost
rewrite, generation lookup, or pricing interpreter. Only usable **reported charges**
count, not Pi catalog estimates, separate upstream inference cost, available credit,
or account activity elsewhere. Amounts are diagnostic floating sums, not invoice
arithmetic. Comparison permits only summation-scale machine roundoff near the
threshold, not a currency-sized grace amount; reported totals remain unchanged.

The existing reader scans at most the newest 20,000 supplied entries, deduplicates
identical request/attempt identities, excludes conflicts/malformed records, and
separates absent/invalid charges and interrupted attempts. Notices disclose these
coverage gaps, scan bounds and current-load unattached observations when known.
Missing counters remain unknown. A reported zero on a free request is not a missing
charge; no usable reported charge is not a zero balance. A below-threshold subtotal
proves no remaining budget. Other providers, direct clients/shell calls, lost
receipts and unobserved account activity remain outside coverage.

Forks/clones can inherit identical history: do not add overlapping files as separate
expenses. Guest-owned records are not tamper-proof billing evidence. A notice is
not a spending cap, account bill or authority to use a paid model.

## Scope, lifecycle and failure

src/pi/cost-watch.mjs holds one optional object: native manager/id, threshold and
armed/triggered/unavailable state. It stores no transcript text, paths, credentials,
accrued-cost history, configuration or session entries. Bind to manager/id because
Pi creates fresh contexts; do not bind to context-object identity or branch leaf.

Tree navigation, compaction, and model/thinking changes within the same session do
not reset it. session_start (startup/new/resume/fork/reload) and session_shutdown
reset it. A changed manager/id independently invalidates it. Returning to a previous
session never resurrects a notice. Every process/extension reload starts off.

The existing agent_settled handler checks the notice before its existing bookkeeping.
Off/triggered/stopped states do no additional settlement entry scan. Require the
pinned boolean aborted field; an aborted run can still have reported charges.
Never abort, change model/tools/thinking/paid policy, queue input, compact, call a
provider, poll credit, start a timer/background worker, or persist notice state.

Notifications are best-effort. Consume the one shot before display to avoid repeated
or reentrant warnings. Catch exceptions and rejected thenables so UI failure cannot
change provider/session outcomes. TUI/RPC uses ui.notify, non-UI uses stderr, never
structured stdout or model messages. Status says notice attempted, not that a user
