The new getter is sampled after a candidate is chosen and after confirmation,
not during catalog browsing, help, --explain, empty results or initial cancellation.
Rerendering the full summary participates in the existing stale-preview check.
Changed active level, either displayed setting, either reasoning declaration, or
known/absent/unknown status declines the pending switch. Unrelated settings do
not. Unknown-to-unknown raw changes and same-valued edits are intentionally not
content-integrity checks; no atomic lock or persisted signature is added.

A stable confirmation still delegates the exact registered model to Pi once.
There is no setThinkingLevel, level override, settings write, prompt submission,
model substitution, paid grant, new provider request, compaction or context edit
from this addition. Native setModel retains its existing authentication check and
session/model/thinking lifecycle; browsing adds none. Notifications stay outside
ordinary model context, and RPC notification delivery has no rendering receipt.

No new model recommendation, retry/budget controller or runtime dependency.
