- Evidence with provenance and applicability: command/cwd and tested scope when
  known; observed versus reported versus historical versus unrun; later relevant
  edits stale a previous pass. Include relevant failed approaches and their actual
  evidence so a new turn need not repeat them blindly.

All six sections remain plain Markdown, not a schema to be enforced at runtime.
The final section asks for one bounded first action, a prerequisite and a progress
signal. Missing prerequisites should be reported, not bypassed by starting a larger
project. A pointer is not an attached file or proof that the replacement can read it.

