## Scope is not collection or execution authority

`/sandbrief` asks the selected model to use only the context it already has: no
additional file reads, tool calls, tests, edits, uploads, delegation or new sessions.
A path in the focus is a relevance hint, not a file attachment, glob or read request.
Missing files and removed context are not reconstructed. No filesystem inventory,
transcript export, persistent index or hidden completion has been introduced.

Those are model instructions, **not a tool permission boundary**. The active native
tools and process permissions do not change. A generated brief can contain errors
or sensitive information; there is no automatic verification or secret scrubbing.
Current user/project instructions still apply. The command does not grant permission
to run a proposed check, contact a provider, install dependencies or spend money.

If current file inspection is needed, use the existing `/sandreview [scope]` or
