ordinary model turns with their existing instructions and permissions; neither is
invoked automatically, and their resources must be loaded. An earlier assistant
claim is not promoted to observed evidence by another model repeating it.

## Native Pi and free/paid OpenRouter remain the owners

The brief template is expanded into an ordinary turn on the existing model. Its
input includes Pi's existing context; asking for a shorter output does not shrink
that input or retroactively avoid this turn's usage. It might itself trigger normal
native compaction/recovery. It is not a workaround for a request already too large
or an assurance that a free quota or paid budget can accommodate it.

The handoff command makes no model call and never selects a model, enables payment,
changes reasoning, copies files, submits the draft or erases the saved source. The
user reviews the new session's model and policy before submitting. Native new-session
