Date: 2026-10-10

## Outcome

This is the first release in this repository whose complete normal room path was
executed on the target NixOS host. The standalone artifact, pinned guest, native
Pi runtime, shared Sandcodex credentials, Nix store transport, persistence, and
provider continuations were tested together. The prior archive remains history;
the source tree and regenerated `sandpi` are the release inputs.

## What changed

- Native Pi 1.1.0 installed-contract fixtures import the exact pinned sibling
  modules and cover chat/messages, free/paid policy, routing hooks, cancellation,
  error evidence, credential recovery, settings, handoff, and runtime lifetime.
- The host store is one read-only virtiofs lower view. The exact durable lease is
  used for database registration, recovery, receipts, and GC roots; it is not
  misrepresented as a filesystem visibility or secrecy boundary.
- One aggregate Nix object references the complete lease. Both host and guest
  root that graph. The guest hides the host-global `.links` directory with a
  persistent opaque directory in the overlay upper layer, keeping dedup hard
  links on the same filesystem.
- Store sharing uses `cache=never`; the service and guest receive large
  descriptor limits. Sandpi reserves a 768 MiB plus per-path backend allowance
  inside the requested room budget and fails before boot when too little remains
  for the guest.
- Checkpoint/digest mutation detection includes allocated block count, catching
  fast extent changes even when timestamp resolution is insufficient.
- Acceptance owns and terminates its process group on interruption. Live VM
  tests use isolated state and empty credential roots except explicit provider
  tests, which read the canonical Sandcodex bank through the normal resolver.

