# Sandpi 0.83.0 release report — Kestrel

Date: 2026-10-10

## Outcome

Kestrel makes a normal repeat boot fast without replacing Sandpi's cold-disk
upgrade boundary or weakening readiness. The first installation still performs
the real Nix build and full database registration. Once that durable state exists,
an unchanged launch verifies it and goes directly to Cloud Hypervisor; a runtime
upgrade exports and imports only a new registration segment.

On this release host, the pre-change 0.82.0 warm one-shot path took 65.554 seconds.
After the cache, guest-init, virtiofs, and readiness changes, the same unchanged
one-shot command took 14.844 seconds, a 77% reduction. An unchanged detached
start took 12.998 seconds and entry into that running room took 0.620 seconds.
The first launch of the final changed source fingerprint took 46.696 seconds
while it built the new guest bundle and appended 13 paths to the retained lease.
These are dated observations on one NixOS machine, not portable performance
promises or release pass/fail thresholds.

## What changed

- `register_cache` validates the retained lease once and recognizes when the
  current bundle is already included. It verifies the path schema, aggregate
  root, owned single-link registration artifacts, and every SHA-256 digest while
  avoiding a fresh Nix evaluation of the complete reference graph.
- Registration is an ordered append-only segment index. A legacy monolithic
  stream becomes segment one. New runtime paths produce one delta stream. The
  guest records each successfully imported segment on its persistent disk and
  hash-checks every unseen segment before `nix-store --load-db`.
- The immutable host store uses virtiofs automatic caching. Existing room budget
  accounting and descriptor limits remain in force; the broader store listing
  remains visible and is not reclassified as an exact filesystem boundary.
- The guest uses NixOS's pinned native `nixos-init`, mutable `/etc` overlay, and
  systemd-sysusers paths. A different toplevel still supplies a different boot
  specification before switch-root, but an unchanged boot no longer replays the
  Bash/Perl activation program through virtiofs.
- Successful kernel/systemd serial chatter is quiet; warnings, failed units,
  panic output, the system journal, and backend logs remain available.
- Readiness polling uses short disposable vsock connections until an SSH banner
  is visible, then performs the existing authenticated room-ID command. A vsock
  control socket, Cloud Hypervisor route acknowledgement, or banner alone cannot
  commit a runtime upgrade.
- `cache_ready.elapsed_seconds`, `cache_ready.fast_path`, and
  `guest_ready.boot_seconds` make repeat-boot regressions diagnosable without
  recording prompts, model output, credentials, Pi arguments, or workspace data.

## Verification

The release gate covers the regenerated standalone artifact and the same pinned
NixOS/Cloud Hypervisor path used by ordinary launches:

| Check | Result | Scope |
|---|---:|---|
| Focused cache/VM contracts | pass | fast path, segment tamper rejection, nixos-init policy, quiet boot argv, banner-gated readiness |
| Pinned Nix contract | pass | guest evaluation/build, NixOS boot artifacts, CH/virtiofsd/passt/Pi versions |
| Existing-room upgrade | pass | cold rollback transaction, new boot spec, writable project, guest Nix executable, authenticated room identity |
| Final warm one-shot | pass | same command as baseline; 72,974-path lease, `fast_path: true`, 0.547-second cache phase, 9.418-second hypervisor-to-ready receipt, 14.844 seconds wall |
| Detached start and running-room entry | pass | 12.998-second start; authenticated command through native vsock/SSH path in 0.620 seconds; 902,959,104-byte observed memory peak |
| Full offline suite and packaged self-test | pass | 73 isolated modules each; reproducible standalone generation and Bash syntax |
| Two-boot VM acceptance | pass | 12 checks: isolated disk, project boundary, Nix install/GC, lower-store survival, restart persistence, teardown |
| Isolated acceptance repeat boot | pass | 73,115-path lease; 0.466-second cache phase and 17.884-second ready time at the deliberately constrained 1-vCPU profile |

Provider requests are outside this performance release. Kestrel does not change
Pi 1.1.0, provider translation, key selection, payment policy, model catalogs, or
native conversation storage. Bedrock's live provider results remain dated prior
evidence rather than being silently relabeled as this release's observations.

## Safety and recovery boundaries

- A missing, foreign-owned, linked, malformed, or digest-mismatched registration
  segment fails closed. Sandpi does not regenerate around corruption on the fast
  path or ask the guest to trust a host marker.
- The lease remains cumulative while any dependent room/checkpoint survives.
  Append-only registration is not automatic cache pruning.
- NixOS `nixos-init` changes how the complete image initializes; it does not make
  the guest immutable. `/etc`, `/nix/store` upper data, Pi sessions, packages,
  and root's home remain persistent room state.
- Initial Nix build/registration cost is still real. `--boot-timeout 600` remains
  deliberately generous for first import and slow hosts.
- An already-running detached room remains the fastest path: later entry avoids
  boot entirely. Sandpi does not silently keep an owner-terminal room alive or
  change its documented resource lifetime merely to improve a benchmark.

