# Rev0028 research: defaults versus native choices

Checked 2026-10-06. Runtime remains Pi 1.0.4 at immutable commit
`7c10bd4337495ee613f2224843ecdf349b80d1df`. Public upstream documentation and
source were read; no Sandcodex expansion was undertaken this revision. Sources
below are first-party documentation or source. No third-party compatibility code
was copied. The conclusions describe this pin, not a permanent Pi API promise.

## Findings and implementation decisions

**Launch intent must not become a permanent thinking lock.** Pi separates current
conversation choices from startup defaults. Its public event contract labels
initial startup separately from reload, new, resume and fork. The existing
Sandpi check ignored that distinction and was also run on model selection and
tree movement. Rev0028 retains final startup validation, then defers later choices
to Pi. This is a correction of our integration, not an upstream bug. [R1, R2]

**Inspect merged settings instead of adding another configuration language.**
`pi.getSettings()` returns effective settings and `ctx.getContextUsage()` exposes
a possibly unknown estimate. These can feed an on-demand report without reading
session files or interpreting project configuration independently. [R2]

**Compaction is more than a threshold.** Pi resolves each exact-model token
setting independently and validates safe nonnegative integers. Its reserve also
influences summary output budgeting. We therefore do not “optimize” all large
paid models by lowering the reserve or introducing an invented quality window.
The helper explains current reserve, retention, estimated threshold and their
sources. Invalid explicit settings are disclosed rather than overwritten. [R3, R4]

**Model sampling and actual requests are different observations.** Pi merges
base model sampler fields, effective-thinking overrides and request overrides.
The supported generic sampler path applies to specified OpenAI-compatible APIs,
not every backend. The report only displays known numeric fields and says later
request hooks may override them. It neither injects sampler values nor copies
arbitrary payload objects into diagnostics. [R1, R6]

**Qualification should test native choices without spending on inference.** RPC
has ID-correlated responses and explicit prompt disposition. A slash command that
is locally handled is distinct from a prompt accepted for a run. The native
acceptance sequence asserts model/thinking state after every boundary and checks
that the fixture server receives no inference requests. A test-only extension
invokes public `ctx.reload()` to exercise reconstruction, rather than imitating a
reload by restarting our stub. [R2, R5]

**Keep existing cache and price policy separate.** OpenRouter session affinity and
price/parameter routing interact with provider choice; they do not imply a reason
to reassert a thinking preference for an entire process. Paid account-group
balancing, exact physical routes, no-replay and inline cost observation are left
byte-identical. This release adds no provider sorting or extra request. [R7, R8]

