**Chat error display can lose origin.** In the pinned Chat Completions adapter,
payload and response hooks execute inside the same request try/catch as the
native SDK work. Stream events also pass through the observer before conversion.
The boundary does not inherently say that a caught error originated remotely.
Sandpi must not infer that solely from diagnostic text. [2]

**Messages has the same composition concern.** Its payload/response hooks and
stream observer are awaited in the request path; the catch block constructs
an assistant error with diagnostic text. A locally thrown JSON-shaped message
