Use a version-distinguishable filename carrying boot/PID/start/nonce identity,
without adding fields to the already-versioned runtime JSON. Retain live and
uncertain records independently of the bounded history of completed commands.
Serialize allocation, reserve a unique filename and bound directory inspection.
Never collect on `session_shutdown`, and do not add a daemon, heartbeat, provider
shim or second session manager. Read no conversation or credential data.

