# Rev0043 research — native model discovery and deliberate switches

Research date: 2026-10-08. Target: Pi 1.1.0, exact commit
`abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7`. These findings were checked online
this turn. They are separate from the supplied archive's implementation and from
its prior release receipts. No live inference or model-performance review was made.

## What the supplied implementation already provided

Rev0042 already had `/sandmodels free|paid`, paid process permission, validated
catalog models, exact/revision-bound recipes, native compaction/cost inspection,
and paid/free request wrappers. The missing workflow was narrowing a large list
and understanding a switch before committing. This revision extends that command;
it does not add a second picker command or another provider registry.

## Upstream contracts checked

### Pi exposes the needed native extension seam

The pinned extension guide describes commands, native model/session controls,
read-only context and UI. The exported types define `getContextUsage()` with a
nullable token estimate, and `ctx.ui.select()`/`ctx.ui.confirm()` for dialogs.
Interactive and RPC clients support these dialogs; terminal custom components
are not equivalent in RPC. This favors the simple native dialogs over a new TUI.

Sources:
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/types.ts
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/docs/rpc-extension-ui.md

### Native dialogs need bounded content

The exact pinned ExtensionSelectorComponent renders every option with a Text
component, with no scrolling list viewport. Native confirm puts its message in
that selector's title. The design therefore uses five-model pages and a compact
confirmation, with the complete report in native UI notification/scrollback.
This is source inspection, not evidence that real terminal layouts were run.

Sources:
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/extension-selector.ts
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts

### Unknown context after compaction is intentional

The native AgentSession implementation returns `tokens: null` when the latest
compaction has no later usable assistant accounting. Otherwise it estimates the
projected context and attaches the active context window. Sandpi must not invent
a zero or treat a previous model's window as current. Candidate comparisons are
explicitly approximate; no tokenizer or session parsing is added.

Source:
- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts

### Native model changes have their own lifecycle

AgentSession.setModel checks native auth, appends the native model change, resolves
thinking for the new model and emits model_select. Global model defaults are
written only with an explicit persistence option. The extension API delegates
through this runtime. The preview should not pre-apply thinking/tools, mutate a
shared model, or persist a second set of model preferences.

Source: the same pinned AgentSession implementation above, model-management and
extension binding sections. Native precedence remains in Pi; the existing
Sandpi inspection helper is reused rather than duplicating it in the picker.

### OpenRouter metadata is useful evidence, not a quality or availability promise

OpenRouter's Models API documents IDs, display names, canonical slugs, context
length, supported parameters, modality metadata and pricing. These support exact
ID search and explicit capability filters. They do not establish a comparative
coding ranking or guarantee that one endpoint can satisfy the next request.

The current pricing schema includes conditional prompt-length and scheduled
changes. The picker therefore displays effective native estimates/known tiers
with an explicit non-invoice label, not a made-up session spend projection.

Source:
- https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/models

### Provider choice and free routing are separate from model browsing

OpenRouter documents provider `require_parameters`, fallback/order preferences
and `max_price`; price ceilings are endpoint-rate constraints, not session budgets.
Its free variant documentation also notes availability/rate limits. A local
model browse should not probe credits, lease keys, change provider sorting, or
assume a `:free` suffix proves the whole pricing policy.

Sources:
- https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/provider-selection
- https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/model-variants/free

## Product choices (design decisions, not upstream requirements)

Keep the default free, keep existing free ordering, and make paid inclusion an
explicit view. Add composable tools/vision/fits/reviewed filters instead of
hard-coding another model leaderboard. Preview before switching; never turn
selection into authorization to spend. Preserve direct native `/model` for users
who do not need this extra preview. No new external dependency or persistence.

A fully automatic router, cheapest-first reranker, auto-compacting model switch,
and automatic paid fallback were considered and rejected for this revision.
Each would change the user's inference or billing intent instead of merely
helping them choose. Native Pi remains the session application.

