# Rev0051 / Reveal — research and design decisions

Research date: 2026-10-08. This is external primary-source research plus an audit of
the exact supplied rev0050 ZIP. Upstream facts below are distinct from Sandpi's
implementation decisions and the local executions recorded in evidence/rev0051/.
Pinned Pi remains 1.1.0, commit abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7.

## 1. Native lookup is not availability or request authentication

Source (pinned):
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/core/model-registry.ts

The synchronous ModelRegistry facade separates find(provider,modelId), getAll(),
getAvailable(), refresh() and getApiKeyAndHeaders(). find delegates to the model
runtime's lookup; getAvailable reads an available snapshot; refresh is async;
auth resolution belongs to a separate API. An ID's native metadata and request-time
authentication are not the same operation.

Sandpi decision: diagnose the exact managed ID set and use native find() for its
effective model metadata. Do not switch to an availability-filtered list, resolve
auth, refresh models, or infer working credentials. Missing native registration is
a local gap, not proof that the upstream model was removed or is unavailable.

## 2. Native overrides and explicit selection remain authoritative

Source (pinned):
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/docs/models.md

models.json supports existing-model metadata overrides without replacing a
provider's list. Unknown override IDs are ignored. /model reloads that native file
on opening. Compatible endpoint configuration is distinct from a verified
compatibility claim; model metadata can vary from a bundled catalog.

Sandpi decision: explanation reads the composed native model for names, image
membership, cost and configured limits. Do not use a cached price/name while the
actual picker uses an override. Missing native models can only be searched by
managed ID and an applicable recipe, not by an invented native display name.
Native /model remains a separate explicit action, not an automatic repair.

## 3. The live model catalog has its own scope

Source (current official documentation):
https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/models

The Models API documents model ID, supported_parameters, modalities, pricing,
context and lifecycle metadata. Its default output filter is text; omitted
non-text models are not evidence of a platform outage. It supports optional
filters/pagination. The documented single-model lookup resolves aliases, but that
is another network operation. Pricing includes units and conditional overrides,
not one universally guaranteed rate for an entire workload.

Sandpi decision: label the inventory as this invocation's managed IDs, not the full
live catalog. No new lookup, pagination, alias resolution or live refresh is added.
An absent ID cannot be distinguished as stale, unloaded, unknown or omitted upstream
by these local facts. Unknown tool support/rates are explicit exclusions where a
filter requires evidence; model quality is not inferred from any of this metadata.
Highest-base/all-tier rate filters remain local estimates, not invoice ceilings.

## 4. Routing constraints are separate from catalog filtering

Source (current official documentation):
https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/provider-selection

OpenRouter describes request-level provider preferences and constraints, including
only/ignore, max_price, support for requested parameters, data policy and fallbacks.
The existence of a model entry does not demonstrate that a particular request can
be served under its constraints. No provider request was used to verify availability
or parameter behavior for this revision.

Sandpi decision: an eligible diagnostic result means eligible for this local picker,
not ready for inference. Local blocked-model markers are not a new provider outage
diagnosis. Preserve route exclusions, paid permission and native model authority;
never automatically retry, probe, relax filters or substitute another route/model.
Other-section search matches are labelled before other filters, not ready choices.

## 5. UI notifications are not conversation messages or acknowledgements

Sources (pinned):
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/docs/rpc-extension-ui.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/earendil-works/pi/abe508e1b89912adde45528136c3221eb69acdd7/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/extension-selector.ts

RPC extensions distinguish request/response dialogs from fire-and-forget UI
notifications. The pinned selector renders its options rather than supplying a
catalog-sized scrolling viewport. A notification's emission is not proof of how a
client renders or preserves it.

Sandpi decision: --explain uses a single UI notification (or stderr without a UI),
not another selector or editor operation, and includes at most five example IDs.
The full aggregate reasons are retained with overlapping-count labels. Explicit
report mode does not wait for idle. Actual terminal scrolling/wrapping, client
