## Rev0021 stopped-room cloning research — 2026-10-06

- **Pi v1.0.4 release and immutable source tag.** The stable release remained
  v1.0.4 at commit `7c10bd4337495ee613f2224843ecdf349b80d1df` during this
  revision; Sandpi keeps the existing pin rather than following mutable main.
  https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/releases/tag/v1.0.4

- **Pi sessions are cwd-grouped native state.** This supports copying session bytes
  only as part of the guest disk while keeping host observations room-scoped and
  leaving conversation parsing to Pi.
  https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/v1.0.4/packages/coding-agent/docs/sessions.md

- **Linux file clone ioctls.** `FICLONE` creates a CoW clone when supported, while
  later writes may allocate independent blocks. Sandpi continues treating reflink
  as an optimization rather than a storage reservation or backup guarantee.
  https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/ioctl_ficlonerange.2.html

- **GNU `cp --reflink` semantics.** The filesystem may share data blocks and copy-
  on-write; unsupported automatic reflink falls back to ordinary copy. Sandpi
  implements the same preference explicitly so it can retain sparse-copy and
  source-stability receipts.
  https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/cp-invocation.html

- **Linux `renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE)`.** Atomic no-replace publication is the
  required target-directory commit primitive. Sandpi fails closed when the host
  cannot provide it instead of using a check-then-rename race.
  https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/rename.2.html

- **Python rename/replace documentation.** `os.replace()` intentionally overwrites,
  while `os.rename()` replacement behavior is platform dependent. This reinforced
  using the Linux no-replace syscall directly for clone publication rather than a
  Python pre-check followed by ordinary rename.
  https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.rename

- **Cloud Hypervisor v53.0 release.** The VMM pin remains 53.0. Rev0021 deliberately
  uses cold guest-disk copying rather than CH memory snapshots, so Pi sessions and
  packages persist without inheriting live VMM/process state.
  https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor/releases/tag/v53.0

