### Linux atomic no-replace rename

- `renameat2(2)` / `RENAME_NOREPLACE`:
  `https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/rename.2.html`

`RENAME_NOREPLACE` atomically refuses an existing target, avoiding a
check-then-rename race. The Linux manual also warns that on NFS an application
cannot assume failure means the rename did not happen. Sandpi therefore writes a
transaction inside the source before publication, lets that transaction follow
the moved directory, and treats durable target metadata plus the final receipt as
the recovery authority. It never falls back to an overwriting rename or a disk
copy under the guise of rename.

