"""Stable host-only project identity and path binding.

The project directory is live host data, while a Sandpi room is a persistent
machine.  A tiny ``PROJECT/.sandpi/project.json`` anchor lets the machine follow a
project when its directory is renamed or moved.  The directory is already masked
from the VM, so the anchor never becomes ordinary guest workspace state.

The first anchor deliberately uses the canonical path as its namespace.  That
preserves every room ID created by earlier Sandpi revisions.  A later move carries
the namespace in the project directory.  A central binding under SANDPI_HOME
prevents a copied ``.sandpi`` directory from silently attaching two live project
copies to the same machine.  It also permits bounded recovery when an ignored-file
cleanup removes the project-local anchor: exact filesystem-object evidence may be
restored automatically, while path-only or ambiguous evidence requires an explicit
operator choice.
"""
